nutau-prop v0.10 CHAT-TAB RECONCILIATION / CANONICAL PHYSICS CHECKPOINT
=====================================================================
Date: 2026-10-27
Author/project owner: Subhendu Rakshit

PURPOSE OF THIS FILE
--------------------
This is a versioned continuation/checkpoint of PROGRESS.log.  It does not
replace, truncate, or rewrite the earlier execution history.  It records the
scientific state reached in the present chat before subsequent work is allowed
to change the interpretation.

CANONICAL PROJECT GOAL
----------------------
The project is about tau-neutrino propagation through the Earth in the
presence of non-standard interactions.  The central question is whether a
physically allowed interaction can produce a sufficiently large and
characteristic propagation distortion to be observable.  The project is NOT
a no-go-theorem project, and it is NOT the separate cosmogenic-neutrino /
UHECR proton-fraction project.

The sequence of this project matters:

1. The historical nu_tau/tau transport machinery was first validated against
   Dutta-Reno-Sarcevic and Rakshit-Reya benchmarks.
2. Smooth charge-radius and derivative/forward-blind interaction benchmarks
   were then propagated through IceCube/ARCA-style observables.  Their
   distortions were too weak or too degenerate with flux normalization/slope
   to provide a useful signal in the tested responses.
3. The user therefore required a qualitatively different interaction with
   genuine momentum enhancement.  This destroyed the earlier smooth-model
   failure: the momentum-growing operator can generate a large high-energy
   cross-section modification.
4. The new problem is not lack of momentum enhancement.  The problem is that
   the same enhancement extends into the UHE/cosmogenic-neutrino regime and
   collides with IceCube/KM3NeT observations/limits.

v0.7 MOMENTUM-GROWING CASE-6 RESULT
----------------------------------
The benchmark is the dimension-seven Case-6 neutrino-quark operator discussed
by Pandey, Karmakar and Rakshit, JHEP 11 (2019) 046,

  L_C6 = C4 (bar nu_i^c <->partial_mu nu_j)(bar q gamma^mu q) + h.c.,

with benchmark coefficient

  C4 = 8.6e-10 GeV^-3.

The PDF-level calculation used CT10nlo and integrated explicitly over Bjorken
x and y with

  shat ~= 2 m_N E_nu x,
  Q^2 = shat y.

Two EFT-domain prescriptions were kept separate:

  PRIMARY / conservative: sqrt(shat) < Lambda_UV,
  AGGRESSIVE envelope:    Q < Lambda_UV.

The aggressive Q cut is not accepted as the primary prediction because small
y can keep Q below Lambda while sqrt(shat) is already outside the EFT domain.

The Mac Studio validation gave

  no-cut sigma_NP/sigma_SM = 5.34e-4 at 0.1 PeV,
                            = 1.38e-2 at 1 PeV.

For the conservative sqrt(shat)<Lambda cut, the important ratios at
E_nu=(1,10,100,300) PeV are:

  Lambda=1.5 TeV: (0.0138, 0.0909, 0.148, 0.177)
  Lambda=2.0 TeV: (0.0138, 0.194,  0.351, 0.434)
  Lambda=2.44TeV: (0.0138, 0.302,  0.569, 0.719)
  Lambda=3.0 TeV: (0.0138, 0.404,  1.03,  1.33)

With c4=C4 Lambda^3, c4/(4pi)=0.231, 0.547, 0.994, 1.848 for
Lambda=1.5,2.0,2.44,3.0 TeV.  Thus 2.44 TeV is already near the nominal 4pi
coefficient diagnostic and 3 TeV is beyond it.

PHYSICS CONCLUSION FROM v0.7
----------------------------
Momentum growth works.  The earlier conclusion obtained from smooth
interactions is not robust against a genuinely momentum-growing operator.
The project therefore moved from the question "can the propagation effect be
made large?" to the question "can the required momentum growth survive UHE
neutrino observations and EFT/laboratory consistency?"

v0.8 UHE / COSMOGENIC OBSERVATIONAL STRESS TEST
-----------------------------------------------
The saved Case-6 cross-section curves were folded against:

  * the official IceCube 12.6-year EHE effective area;
  * the official KM3NeT KM3-230213A bright-track effective area;
  * the public Ehlert cosmogenic-neutrino spectral shape as a fixed benchmark
    shape for this stress test.

The Ehlert spectrum is used here only to expose the UHE observational tension.
This does not turn nutau-prop into the separate cosmogenic proton-fraction
project.

KM3NeT validation was excellent:

  calculated full 335-d expectation = 0.242754,
  official notebook benchmark       = 0.242767,

and in the published central-90% parent-energy range:

  calculated = 0.211081,
  official   = 0.211117.

ICECUBE UNIT BUG AND CORRECTION
-------------------------------
The first v0.8 IceCube parser treated the headerless first numerical row as
column names and therefore missed the conversion of the official effective
area from m^2 to cm^2.  This produced the false SM result 0.001767 events.
An attempted in-place NumPy conversion then failed because the returned array
was read-only.  The corrected copy()*1e4 conversion gives

  IceCube EHE Ehlert SM, 12.6 yr = 17.674595 events.

This bug is part of the project history and must not be hidden.

CORRECTED v0.8 PRIMARY EVENT-PROXY TABLE
---------------------------------------
Using the conservative sqrt(shat)<Lambda cross-section enhancement in the
inclusive IceCube response proxy:

  Lambda [TeV]   N_IC(SM)   N_IC(SM+NP proxy)   fractional increase
  -----------------------------------------------------------------
     1.50         17.67          20.73                0.173
     2.00         17.67          25.05                0.417
     2.44         17.67          31.15                0.763
     3.00         17.67          42.54                1.407

The corresponding aggressive Q<Lambda proxy gives 37.73, 61.93, 92.85 and
145.9 events and is retained only as an upper-envelope diagnostic.

The important physical result is that the same momentum enhancement that
makes the propagation effect interesting also strongly enhances the UHE
response where IceCube has very restrictive observations.

COMMON-FLUX SCREEN USED AT v0.8
-------------------------------
At this stage a deliberately crude zero-count Poisson scale

  kappa_90 = 2.302585 / N_IC

was used only as a screening diagnostic.  It is NOT the published IceCube EHE
likelihood and it is NOT a model-specific 90% confidence limit.

After applying this common-flux screening normalization, the KM3NeT
NC-equivalent response proxy becomes almost independent of Lambda:

  N_KM3^(screen) ~= 0.0315, 0.0314, 0.0312, 0.0310

for Lambda=1.5,2.0,2.44,3.0 TeV.

This near-cancellation is understood analytically.  For a common flux
normalization kappa,

  N_IC = kappa I,     N_KM3 = kappa K,

so a constraint kappa <= U/I implies

  N_KM3 <= U K/I.

If the same interaction enhances both UHE acceptances similarly, the ratio
K/I changes much less than either absolute yield.

TOPOLOGY CAVEAT: CASE 6 IS NC-LIKE
----------------------------------
The Case-6 hard final state is neutrino-sector plus hadrons.  It does not
produce the charged muon required for a direct bright-track event.  Therefore
multiplying the KM3NeT bright-track effective area by (1+r) is only an
NC-equivalent acceptance proxy and must never be called a direct track
prediction.

At the screened common-flux scales, the unchanged direct bright-track
expectation is approximately

  0.027, 0.022, 0.018, 0.013

for Lambda=1.5,2.0,2.44,3.0 TeV, respectively, in the original v0.8
screening estimate.

CANONICAL v0.8 INTERPRETATION
-----------------------------
The correct statement at this checkpoint is:

  Momentum growth survives at the cross-section / propagation level, but the
  same growth clashes with the UHE/cosmogenic observational constraint when
  folded through IceCube and KM3NeT response proxies.

This is NOT a no-go theorem.  It is the identification of the central tension
for the momentum-enhanced nutau-propagation idea.

WHAT v0.8 DID NOT ESTABLISH
---------------------------
1. The 2.3026-event normalization is only a screen.  IceCube's 12.6-year EHE
   analysis uses reconstructed energy and direction, background/nuisance
   components and pseudoexperiment calibration.
2. The public all-flavor IceCube effective area is a Standard-Model detector
   response.  Multiplying it by an inclusive cross-section ratio is a proxy,
   not a complete BSM detector simulation.
3. The KM3NeT bright-track response cannot be used as the acceptance for the
   Case-6 NC hard interaction.
4. A tau-specific interaction cannot automatically rescale every flavor in the
   published IceCube all-flavor area.
5. No exact EHE binned likelihood was available from the public release
   inspected in this project.

NEXT STEP IDENTIFIED AT THIS CHECKPOINT
---------------------------------------
The next calculation was therefore fixed: replace the crude 2.3026-event
screen by IceCube's published energy-dependent EHE information as faithfully
as the public release allows, while keeping the limitations explicit.  This
became the subsequent v0.9 public-data diagnostic.  The v0.9 refinement is a
later stage; it does not erase or change the v0.8 discovery of the central
momentum-growth versus UHE-observation tension.

SCOPE LOCK FOR FUTURE WORK
--------------------------
Future work in this repository must preserve the project identity:

  * primary subject: tau-neutrino propagation through Earth with BSM
    interactions;
  * current successful mechanism: genuine momentum enhancement;
  * current obstacle: UHE/cosmogenic observational consistency of that
    enhancement;
  * KM3NeT/IceCube are observational constraints/diagnostics, not a change of
    the project into a KM3-event-explanation paper;
  * the separate cosmogenic-neutrino/UHECR proton-fraction project must not be
    imported into this repository's scientific goal.

No new numerical computation is claimed in this checkpoint file.  It records
and reconciles the already executed v0.7/v0.8 results from the chat and the
repository history.
